Hello everyone,

I am happy to announce that we now have a web site dedicated
to the kernel perfmon subsystem, the libpfm library and the 
pfmon tool.

For each component, the web site includes a simple overview, 
full documentation, lots of code examples, and a FAQ section. 
The perfmon site is at: 

       http://www.hpl.hp.com/research/linux/perfmon

In addition, we have also setup a mailing list to discuss 
performance monitoring on Linux/ia64. 

The list is open to everyone with an interest in using/developing 
performance monitoring tools and IS NOT limited to the pfmon/libpfm 
packages. To limit spam, you need to be a subcriber to the list to be 
allowed to post.  

To subscribe follow the instructions on the perfmon web site at:

	http://www.hpl.hp.com/research/linux/perfmon/mail.php4

Enjoy,
